From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000019 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Port Bot <port@local>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 13:00:03 +0200
Subject: 0019: flag-gate the core Pod Terminal tab

Add a POD_TERMINAL_PLUGIN_FLAG (TERMINAL_PLUGIN_POD_TERMINAL_ENABLED)
check to PodsDetailsPage's pages array, mirroring
0020-node-terminal-flag-gate.patch's identical pattern for the Node
Terminal tab. When the terminal console plugin's own backend reports
POD_TERMINAL_ENABLED=true, it sets this flag via a console.flag extension
and contributes its own Pod Terminal tab (a console.tab/horizontalNav
extension, which can only add a tab, never replace one) - this patch is
the other half of that pair, letting core step aside so exactly one Pod
Terminal tab is ever shown. Unset (the default, and the only possible
state on a console without that plugin) leaves this tab exactly as it
was.

Supersedes 0019-pod-connect-transport-extension.patch: that patch
augmented core's own Terminal tab with a pluggable-transport extension
point (used to merge VNC connections into core's dropdown). Now that the
terminal plugin owns its Pod Terminal tab outright rather than augmenting
core's, that extension point has no remaining consumer and core goes back
to being fully unmodified for the merge/transport concern - this patch
only ever toggles the tab's presence, nothing about its contents.
